<section class="hero arch-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
  <h1>Simple parts.<br><span class="grad">Clear boundaries.</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">spendlens is a Python CLI that turns AWS APIs into SQL with Steampipe, runs your company's controls with
    Powerpipe, and keeps every result in a local history that reports, the executive brief, notifications and the AI
    assistant read. For live questions the assistant works from a catalog of the AWS plugin's 589 tables.</p>
  <ul class="stack-strip" aria-label="Built with">
    <li>Python</li><li>Steampipe</li><li>Powerpipe</li><li>SQLite</li><li>Jinja2</li><li>sqlglot</li>
    <li>Anthropic SDK</li><li>OpenAI SDK</li><li>AWS plugin catalog</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section showcase arch" id="context">
  <div class="wrap sc stack">
    <div class="sc-text">
      <div class="sc-title">
        <p class="t-eyebrow">C4 · Level 1</p>
        <h2>Who uses it.<br>What it talks to.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="sc-copy">
        <p>People and pipelines ask the cost questions; spendlens reads AWS, optionally asks an LLM, and posts summaries
          to chat. Every arrow into AWS is a read.</p>
        <ul class="chips"><li>Read-only towards AWS</li><li>No agents</li><li>No SaaS</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sc-media">{{ diagram("c4_context") }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section showcase arch alt" id="containers">
  <div class="wrap sc stack">
    <div class="sc-text">
      <div class="sc-title">
        <p class="t-eyebrow">C4 · Level 2</p>
        <h2>What runs inside.<br>How data moves.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="sc-copy">
        <p>Controls run through Powerpipe, cost questions go straight to Steampipe as bounded SQL, and every run lands
          in a SQLite history that the dashboard, the executive brief, notifications and the AI assistant read without
          touching AWS again.</p>
        <ul class="chips"><li>{{ stats.controls }} controls</li><li>One history</li><li>Pluggable</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sc-media">{{ diagram("c4_container") }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="principles">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="h2">Four design decisions.</h2>
    <p class="sub">The choices that keep spendlens small, predictable and easy to extend.</p>
    <div class="bento arch-bento">
      <article class="tile t-wide">
        <span class="tile-ico" aria-hidden="true">{{ icons["list"]|safe }}</span>
        <p class="t-eyebrow">Controls via Powerpipe</p>
        <h3>Your standards, as SQL controls.</h3>
        <p>Tag, rightsizing and waste rules are controls in a bundled Powerpipe mod. Thresholds live in
          <code>finops.yaml</code> and are passed in as mod variables, so one file holds your company standards, and
          every control's SQL is checked offline against the AWS plugin's schema.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tile">
        <span class="tile-ico" aria-hidden="true">{{ icons["chart"]|safe }}</span>
        <p class="t-eyebrow">Cost via direct SQL</p>
        <h3>Bounded queries.</h3>
        <p>Cost diff, trend, showback, anomalies and forecast query Steampipe's Cost Explorer tables directly, bounded
          to exactly the periods they need.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tile">
        <span class="tile-ico" aria-hidden="true">{{ icons["clock"]|safe }}</span>
        <p class="t-eyebrow">History as the hub</p>
        <h3>Collect once, read often.</h3>
        <p>Every run is saved to SQLite with its findings, cost rows, parameters and CI metadata. Reports and the
          assistant work offline from it.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tile t-wide">
        <span class="tile-ico" aria-hidden="true">{{ icons["puzzle"]|safe }}</span>
        <p class="t-eyebrow">Plugins everywhere</p>
        <h3>Built-ins use the same registry as yours.</h3>
        <p>Commands, Powerpipe mods, savings estimators, AI tools, doctor checks and dashboard tabs all register
          through one plugin API. A broken plugin is reported, never fatal.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section showcase arch alt" id="cli">
  <div class="wrap sc stack">
    <div class="sc-text">
      <div class="sc-title">
        <p class="t-eyebrow">How a command runs</p>
        <h2>Five stages.<br>One flag family each.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="sc-copy">
        <p>Every command, from <code>tags</code> to <code>report</code>, works the same way. It <b>resolves settings</b>
          from four layers, <b>picks a data source</b>, <b>runs</b> controls or cost SQL, <b>saves</b> the run to the
          local history, and <b>prints or writes</b> the result. Learn the flags for one command and you know them for
          all.</p>
        <ul class="chips"><li>Same flags everywhere</li><li>AWS only with --source live</li><li>Every run saved</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sc-media">{{ diagram("cli_flow") }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="flags">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="t-eyebrow center">Common flags</p>
    <h2 class="h2">What each flag changes.</h2>
    <p class="sub">These work on every check and cost command. Run any command with <code>--help</code> for its own
      filters.</p>
    <div class="arch-table-wrap"><table class="arch-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Flag</th><th>What it does</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>1 · Config</td><td><code>-c, --config</code></td><td>The policy file with your company standards. Default
          <code>./finops.yaml</code>, then <code>~/.config/spendlens/finops.yaml</code>.</td>
          <td><code>-c prod/finops.yaml</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>1 · Config</td><td><code>-s, --set</code></td><td>Override one setting for this run only; it beats the
          file and <code>SPENDLENS__</code> environment variables. Repeatable.</td>
          <td><code>--set sizing.ec2_cpu_low=10</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>1 · Config</td><td><code>--var</code></td><td>A raw Powerpipe mod variable that has no
          <code>finops.yaml</code> key.</td><td><code>--var my_threshold=5</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>2 · Source</td><td><code>--source live</code></td><td>Query AWS now through Steampipe (read-only) and save
          the run. The default for checks.</td><td><code>spendlens waste</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>2 · Source</td><td><code>--source last</code></td><td>Reuse the latest saved run. No AWS calls, instant.
          The default for <code>ask</code>.</td><td><code>spendlens tags --source last</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>2 · Source</td><td><code>--source demo</code></td><td>Bundled sample data, to try spendlens without an AWS
          account.</td><td><code>spendlens review --source demo</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>2 · Source</td><td><code>-p, --profile</code></td><td>Which AWS profile Steampipe uses. Default: the
          credentials already in your terminal or CI.</td><td><code>-p finops-readonly</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>3 · Run</td><td><code>--check</code>, <code>--status</code>, <code>-g</code>, <code>--skip</code></td>
          <td>Narrow what runs or what is shown: one tag check, only alarms, cost grouped by service, a dashboard
          without the tag section.</td><td><code>spendlens cost diff -g service</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>5 · Output</td><td><code>-f, --format</code></td><td><code>table</code> (default), <code>csv</code>,
          <code>json</code> or <code>html</code>.</td><td><code>-f csv -o tags.csv</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>5 · Output</td><td><code>-o, --out</code></td><td>Write to a file instead of the screen.</td>
          <td><code>-o review.html</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>5 · Output</td><td><code>--fail-on-alarm</code></td><td>Exit with code 3 if anything is in alarm, to fail
          a CI job.</td><td><code>spendlens tags --fail-on-alarm</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p class="arch-note">See the effective settings and where each came from with <code>spendlens params</code>; check
      your setup with <code>spendlens doctor</code>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section showcase arch alt" id="graph">
  <div class="wrap sc stack">
